The '''Time Pocket''' is a [[Bag]] that appears in the Your Bags menu once the player has reached {{Coll|Timite 2}}. It can also be accessed with the {{Code|/timebag}}, {{Code|/timep}}, {{Code|/timepocket}} or {{Code|/tb}} commands if a {{Item|Booster Cookie}} is active. It is used to store [[Aging Items]], making them age twice as fast.

== Obtaining ==
The '''Time Pocket''' is automatically unlocked once the player reaches {{Coll|Timite 2}}.

=== Upgrading ===
The '''Time Pocket''' can be upgraded from {{Green|6}} to {{Green|9}} slots for {{Item|Discrite|amount=1}}. It can then be further upgraded from {{Green|9}} to {{Green|12}} slots for {{Item|Spotlite|amount=1}}.

== Usage ==
The '''Time Pocket''' stores items that can evolve over time, called '''Aging Items'''. The following items can be stored:
* {{Item|Bottle of Jyrre}} and {{Item|Refined Bottle of Jyrre}}
* {{Item|Dark Cacao Truffle}} and {{Item|Refined Dark Cacao Truffle}}
* {{Item|Discrite}} and {{Item|Spotlite}}
* {{Item|Moby-Duck}} and {{ID|Moby-Duck: Collector's Edition}}
* {{Item|Rosewater Flask}} and {{Item|Filled Rosewater Flask}}
* {{Item|Not Very Moldy Bread}} and {{Item|Very Moldy Bread}}

Items in the '''Time Pocket''' evolve twice as fast, meaning an item that normally takes {{Green|300}} hours to evolve only takes {{Green|150}} hours. Completing the [[Catacombs Puzzle Rooms#Quiz|Quiz]] puzzle in Dungeons will also add {{Green|2}} hours instead of {{Green|1}} to each item in the '''Time Pocket''' (with the exceptions of {{Item|Rosewater Flask}}s, which are unaffected by the puzzle). The effect of {{Item|Enchanted Clock}} is also doubled.

